Revision history for MCP-ArcRaiders

{{$NEXT}}
  - New tools get_ermal (offers and permanent services), get_hideout (stations
    and what each level needs, optionally one station or level) and
    get_weekly_trials (running and coming trials with their time window), each
    with its REST route and OpenAPI path
  - Pendola Pass is selectable: the map choices of get_map_data follow
    WWW::MetaForge::ArcRaiders->maps in the MCP tool and in the OpenAPI
    description; the categories nature and quests are selectable too
  - get_event_timers and get_active_events take a region (europe,
    north-america, oceania, east-asia, brazil or all); events carry their region
  - get_item_details also returns what recycles into an item, which ARCs drop
    it, its mods and locations, flavor text, subcategory, ammo and shield type;
    get_arcs returns the ARC data with its variants; get_quest_details returns
    description, additional rewards and the manifest; map markers carry
    community, source_id and route_id
  - get_quests returns a short overview of all quests over all pages (id, name,
    trader, XP, number of required items and rewards), narrowed by trader or
    name; the new get_quest_details returns one quest by id or name in full,
    with description, objectives, rewards and manifest
  - find_item_seller also finds the items Ermal offers, with coin cost, offer
    period and accepted items, and has its REST route
    (GET /api/items/:name/sellers) and OpenAPI path
  - The trader answer, with Ermal's offers, is cached for an hour
  - The tools hand over characters and the MCP framework encodes the response to
    UTF-8 once; names with a typographic apostrophe reach the
    client intact
  - The server names MetaForge (https://metaforge.app/arc-raiders) as the source of
    the data in its MCP instructions, the OpenAPI description, the info page,
    README and POD
  - The REST routes answer with the same shapers as the MCP tools
  - The offline suite runs on live copies of the MetaForge responses and never
    touches the network; USE_LIVE_API=1 prove -lv t/live.t runs every tool once
    against the real API
  - The tools return the item, ARC, quest, trader and event fields of
    WWW::MetaForge 0.003: items carry item_type, value, stat_block,
    workbench, components, recycle_components and sold_by; ARCs carry
    their loot; quests carry trader_name, xp, nested rewards and guide_url;
    events carry their icon and time slots as ISO 8601 UTC start/end pairs;
    map markers carry id, coordinates, loot_areas and behind_locked_door
  - get_item_details and /api/items/:name list the crafting components and
    used_in (id, name, quantity of each item the item goes into)
  - riven-tides is a selectable map
  - Initial release
  - Tools: search_items, get_item_details, get_arcs, get_quests,
    get_traders, find_item_seller, get_event_timers, get_active_events,
    get_map_data, list_maps
  - The release builds, tags (latest, <major>, <version>) and pushes the
    raudssus/mcp-arcraiders Docker image through the bundle's
    Dist::Zilla::Plugin::Docker::API (docker_image in dist.ini). Every dzil
    build or dzil test builds the image unless DZIL_DOCKER_API_SKIP=1 is set.
